---
source: crates/franken-node/tests/cli_subcommand_goldens.rs
---
franken-node: trust-native JavaScript[PATH] runtime platform

Usage: franken-node <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init            Bootstrap config, policy profile, and workspace metadata
  run             Run app under policy-governed runtime controls
  runtime         Local default lane snapshot and integer epoch compare (not a live node)
  safe-mode       Safe-mode operator lifecycle; persist is unsigned JSON (not Ed25519-signed)
  proofs          Proof-pipeline snapshot[PATH] inspection and restart-request artifacts (not a live broker)
  migrate         Migration audit, rewrite, and validation (rollback JSON is unsigned; validate is not lockstep)
  migrate-report  Export one-command migration assessment report
  verify          Local verification family (Node is the lockstep spec when included; matching only Bun stays fail)
  trust           Local trust-card registry, OSV scan, and file-transport quarantine log
  remotecap       Ed25519 capability tokens; `use` is dry-run (does not send HTTP)
  trust-card      Local trust-card registry inspect (show[PATH]; not a live HTTP API)
  fleet           Local file-transport fleet[PATH] log (not a live control plane)
  incident        Recorded incident bundles: export, integrity-verified replay, counterfactual (not live re-execution)
  ltv             Long-term verifiability attestation and offline verification
  ops             Local ops snapshots: health files, config audit, metrics, corpus run (not a live daemon)
  registry        Local on-disk signed-artifact registry (not a live npm[PATH] service)
  bench           Benchmark suite; report is SHA256 `provenance_hash` (not Ed25519-signed)
  debug           Local artifact debug: receipt explain, evidence inspect, fixture policy-activation trace
  doctor          Local diagnostics: config[PATH], close-condition, evidence snapshot, workspace pressure, bwrap
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
